The authors' reference code (PyTorch research scripts and notebooks for the
paper's experiments) is at https://github.com/WilliamMoriaty/ZENN.

Differences from the authors' reference code:
  - Packaged as sklearn-compatible estimators (ZENNClassifier, ZENNRegressor,
    ZENNRegressorNLL) built on JAX/Flax instead of per-experiment PyTorch
    scripts.
  - Configuration entropy is kept non-negative with softplus(net) rather
    than net**2.
  - ZENNRegressor defaults to a negative log-likelihood (NLL) loss in which
    sigma^2 = sum_k p_k S_k, so the entropy networks also act as a noise
    model. This is an addition, not part of the paper. MSE, hybrid, and
    Jensen-Shannon losses are also available.
  - Adds uncertainty tools (aleatoric/epistemic decomposition, prediction
    intervals, calibration metrics, OOD scores, selective prediction), a
    Chebyshev KAN backbone option, and critical-point/bifurcation analysis.

